  m_Name: 1 - Scan
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: UtilityScriptIWrite::HintSO
  hintId: tutorial_scan
  isUnlockedByDefault: 0
  ignoreLock: 1
  title: Scan
  image: {fileID: 0}
  description: 'The <font="JetBrainsMono SDF"><color=#33CC66>scan</color>()</font>
    command detects the tile directly in front of the robot.

    <font="JetBrainsMono
    SDF"><color=#33CC66>scan</color>()</font> is a command that returns a result.
    The result is a <font="JetBrainsMono SDF"><color=#4FC3F7>str</color></font> (String)
    value describing what is currently detected.


    Examples of common usage:

    <indent=2em>-
    Store the result in a variable: <font="JetBrainsMono SDF">tile <color=#D4D4D4>=</color>
    <color=#33CC66>scan</color>()</font></indent>

    <indent=2em>- Print the result
    directly: <font="JetBrainsMono SDF"><color=#F5F5AB>print</color>(<color=#33CC66>scan</color>())</font></indent>


    Using
    <font="JetBrainsMono SDF"><color=#33CC66>scan</color>()</font> is important because
    it allows the robot to gather information about the environment before making
    any decisions.'
  isImageBig: 0
